Explanation:
- The Bit interacts with the Transmission (to transmit torque), Motor (to receive power), Electrical System (for control and operation), Battery Holder (indirectly through the electrical system for power), Housing (for support and protection), and External Environment (as it comes into contact during use).
- The Transmission interacts with the Motor (to receive power) and the Bit (to transmit torque).
- The Motor interacts with the Electrical System (for control and operation) and the Transmission (to provide power).
- The Electrical System interacts with the Battery Holder (for power), Motor (for control and operation), and External Environment (as it may be affected by external conditions like moisture or dust).
- The Battery Holder only interacts with the Electrical System for providing power.
- The Housing interacts with the Bit, Transmission, Motor, and Electrical System to provide support and protection.
- The External Environment interacts with the Bit (during use), Electrical System (as it may be affected by external conditions like moisture or dust), and Housing (for protection against environmental factors).
